* Targeting
* Keywords, city, radius
* Age, interests, city
---
* Best for
* Services, urgent needs, B2B
* Visual products, desire, novelties
---
* Key metric
* Cost per call or enquiry
* Cost per message or order
{% /table %}

## Budget: two lines not to confuse

A campaign always has two costs. The media budget, paid directly to Google or Meta, which pays for impressions and clicks: plan at least MAD 2,000 to 3,000 a month so the campaigns have enough data to learn. And management fees, which pay for design and running: at Wevtex, MAD 200 a day, whether we run one channel or Google and Meta together.

## The trap that wastes half the clicks

The click is paid for, but the sale happens on the page that receives it. Sending an ad to a general homepage, slow or without a visible WhatsApp button, means paying for visits that leave. Every campaign deserves its landing page: one message, one offer, one button.

## How to know what works

The right indicator isn't the number of clicks but the cost of a lead or a sale. It requires tracking installed before launch: forms, calls and WhatsApp messages counted and attributed to the campaign that generated them. Without it, you optimize by feel.
